  "sourceNote": "This project preserves the station locations, management levels, and click details embedded in Environmental Reporting BC's June 2026 ozone map. It reuses the same seven-zone boundary shared by the Province's PM₂.₅, SO₂, and NO₂ indicator maps. The Province's open ozone-caaqs-indicator repository documents the underlying R analysis and output workflow.",
  "details": [
    "Click or tap an air zone or monitoring station to inspect the Province's 2022–2024 assessment details.",
    "The ozone metric is the three-year average of the annual fourth-highest daily maximum eight-hour rolling concentration.",
    "Management levels use metrics adjusted for approved transboundary flows and exceptional events."
